  "title": "Disaster in Nepal Amid Flash Floods and Landslide",
  "summary": "A flash flood in Arunachal Pradesh and a major landslide at a road construction site in Upper Subansiri district resulted in five Army personnel missing and four people dead. In Nepal, a collapsed glacier caused devastating floods, highlighting the issue of Himalayan ice melting.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Five Army personnel went missing after a flash flood in Arunachal Pradesh's Dibang Valley district, while four people died in a major landslide at a road construction site in Upper Subansiri district.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "A landslide at a road construction site in Upper Subansiri district resulted in four people dead and five Army personnel missing.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Scientists have concluded that a collapsed glacier is the likely cause of the disaster, as it led to devastating floods.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
